Keep the OpenMP team size fixed with libomp unless threads sleep at once.

XGBoost master caps each ParallelFor's team at its loop size and each ParallelFor2d's at its block
count. With LLVM's libomp and a positive blocktime (KMP_BLOCKTIME, which winnowr sets for
training), idle threads wait for the next region, and changing the team size from region to region
costs more than the caps save. This keeps the team at the requested size when the calling thread's
blocktime is positive, and keeps the caps when it is 0 (libomp's default on Apple Silicon, where
threads sleep at once and the caps save wake-ups). It extends patch 0001, which does the same for
libgomp. Results are unchanged.

Source: dmlc/xgboost#12855, commit 7f89ec3f1 (on 293cad1a8 plus f9bd38e6a, the commit patch 0001
carries). Only the src/ hunks are carried here: build.rs builds XGBoost's sources, not its C++
tests, which are in the upstream PR.

Applied by build.rs to a copy of the vendored sources (paths are relative to the XGBoost root),
after patch 0001.

diff --git a/src/common/openmp_exec.h b/src/common/openmp_exec.h
index 3c8cae26d..e765ed82a 100644
--- a/src/common/openmp_exec.h
+++ b/src/common/openmp_exec.h
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@
